        "original_id": "e265d00c-b4bd-5ada-82f3-111bf30e956e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alamgir, Ali Azmat, Meesha Shafi, Strings, Shahzad Hasan\n- Products: Music Icons, Aaina, \"Yaaro Yehi Dosti Hai\"\n- Organizations: ARY Digital\n- Topics: Pakistani music, television, film soundtrack\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Alamgir produced the musical album Aaina from the soundtrack of the Urdu-language Pakistani film of the same name.\n- Ali Azmat was born on April 20, 1970, and he is a Pakistani singer-songwriter, musician, and actor.\n- In the early 1990s, \"Yaaro Yehi Dosti Hai,\" sung by Ali Azmat as one of the Jupiters vocalists, topped the charts and remained a famous song.\n- In April 2013, Alamgir joined Meesha Shafi, Strings, Ali Azmat, and Shahzad Hasan as a judge on Music Icons.\n- Music Icons aired on the ARY Digital TV channel and was described as an immensely popular singing talent show.",
